---
import ExplorerLayout from '../../../layouts/ExplorerLayout.astro';
---
<ExplorerLayout title="Set-up" active="admin">
  <p class="eyebrow">Owner only</p>
  <h1>Set-up and checks</h1>
  <div class="xp-grid">
    <div>
      <section class="xp-panel"><h2>1. Database</h2><div id="mig">Checking…</div><button id="migrate" hidden>Apply the database schema</button><div id="migmsg"></div></section>
      <section class="xp-panel"><h2>2. Import an evidence release</h2>
        <p class="muted small">Choose the three files of one release exported by the engine. They are checked here first (contract, counts, SHA-256), then again on the server. A release is immutable once imported.</p>
        <label for="f-manifest">release.json</label><input type="file" id="f-manifest" accept=".json,application/json" />
        <label for="f-records">records.json</label><input type="file" id="f-records" accept=".json,application/json" />
        <label for="f-cases">cases.json</label><input type="file" id="f-cases" accept=".json,application/json" />
        <button id="check">Check the files</button> <button id="import" disabled>Import the release</button>
        <div id="impmsg"></div></section>
      <section class="xp-panel"><h2>3. Import a corroboration supplement</h2>
        <p class="muted small">A supplement file built by the engine for an imported release (contract bre-supplement/1): sequence-matched GenBank collections and iNaturalist observations for each review case. It is checked against the release's pinned hashes and refused if it contains any location fields. Supplements are immutable once imported.</p>
        <label for="f-supp">Supplement (.json)</label><input type="file" id="f-supp" accept=".json,application/json" />
        <button id="scheck">Check the file</button> <button id="simport" disabled>Import the supplement</button>
        <div id="smsg"></div></section>
      <section class="xp-panel"><h2>4. Import a genus question set</h2>
        <p class="muted small">The decision queue of a genus review report, exported by the engine (contract bre-questions/1, file questions.json). It is checked here and again on the server. A question set is immutable once imported; a new report of the same genus is a new set, and its questions show any earlier decided answer.</p>
        <label for="f-qs">questions.json</label><input type="file" id="f-qs" accept=".json,application/json" />
        <button id="qcheck">Check the file</button> <button id="qimport" disabled>Import the question set</button>
        <div id="qmsg"></div></section>
      <section class="xp-panel"><h2>5. Decision ledgers</h2>
        <p class="muted small">Download a report's decision ledger (contract bre-ledger/1) for the engine's next run. Each download is recorded in the audit log.</p>
        <div id="ledgers" class="muted small">No question sets yet.</div></section>
      <section class="xp-panel"><h2>Production readiness checks</h2>
        <p class="muted small">Runs from your signed-in browser against this deployment. It does not change any data.</p>
        <button id="selftest" class="secondary">Run the checks</button><div id="stmsg"></div></section>
    </div>
    <div>
      <section class="xp-panel"><h2>Reviewers</h2>
        <p class="muted small">Every review and answer is a test until you enable formal reviews for that person, including yourself. Genera: leave empty to let a reviewer answer genus questions for every genus, or list the genera they may answer for (for example: Galerina, Pholiota).</p>
        <div class="xp-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>Role</th><th>Formal</th><th>Active</th><th>Genera</th></tr></thead><tbody id="revs"></tbody></table></div>
        <label for="r-email">E-mail</label><input type="email" id="r-email" />
        <label for="r-name">Display name</label><input type="text" id="r-name" />
        <label for="r-role">Role</label><select id="r-role"><option>reviewer</option><option>observer</option></select>
        <button id="r-add" class="secondary">Add reviewer</button><div id="rmsg"></div>
        <div id="invite" hidden><p class="muted small">Send this to the person (copy it into an e-mail). Before they can sign in, their e-mail must also be allowed by the Cloudflare Access policy of the Explorer, unless the policy already admits any e-mail with a one-time PIN.</p>
          <textarea id="inviteText" rows="9" readonly></textarea><button id="inviteCopy" class="secondary" type="button">Copy the invitation</button></div></section>
      <section class="xp-panel"><h2>Audit log</h2><div class="xp-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>When</th><th>Who</th><th>Action</th><th>Object</th></tr></thead><tbody id="audit"></tbody></table></div></section>
    </div>
  </div>
</ExplorerLayout>
<script>
import '../../../scripts/explorer/admin.js';
</script>
